.\" Manual page for metadata.py. Keep in sync with README.md and "metadata.py --help".
.TH METADATA.PY 1 "2026-10-26" "metadata.py 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
metadata.py \- collect and present metadata for video and image files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B metadata.py
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FORMAT ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR ORDER ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR KIND ]
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-k
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-x ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR CHAR ]
.RB [ \-w ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-\-doubtful\-count
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-doubtful\-seconds
.IR S ]
.RI [ folder ]
.br
.B metadata.py
.RB ( \-c " | " \-v " | " \-h )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B metadata.py
analyzes the video and image files in a folder, and optionally in all of its
subfolders, and presents their metadata on the screen, as a text file, as a CSV
file or as an Excel workbook.
It replaces four earlier scripts (meta.py, metas.py, metas2.py, metax.py).
.PP
For videos it reports container, resolution, duration, video codec, bitrate (kb/s),
frame rate, audio codec, size and file dates.
For images it reports format, resolution, colour mode, size, file dates, the EXIF
date taken and camera, GPS position when present, and an EXIF check
(see
.BR "EXIF CHECK" ).
.PP
.I folder
defaults to the current directory.
It may be given before or after the options.
No argument is mandatory:
.B metadata.py
by itself lists the current folder, without subfolders, on the screen.
.PP
Switches are case-insensitive
.RB ( \-R
is the same as
.BR \-r ,
.B \-\-Recursive
the same as
.BR \-\-recursive )
and every option has a unix-style long form;
.BI \-\-name= value
is accepted as well as
.BI \-\-name " value" .
Only the prerequisites needed for the files found and the outputs chosen are required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Include all subfolders.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFORMAT\fR"
Where to write the result:
.BR screen " (default), " txt ", " csv " or " xlsx .
Give several as a comma-separated list or by repeating the option,
for example
.B \-o txt,xlsx
or
.BR "\-o txt \-o xlsx" .
Files are written to the current directory as
\fIbasename\fR.txt, \fIbasename\fR.csv and \fIbasename\fR.xlsx.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sort " \fIORDER\fR"
.B name
orders by file name only, showing the folder in front of the name.
.B folder
orders by folder and then file name, with a summary for each folder.
The default is
.B folder
together with
.BR \-r ,
otherwise
.BR name .
Without
.B \-r
there is only one folder and
.B folder
has no effect.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-type " \fIKIND\fR"
.BR video ", " image " or " all
(default).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-exif\-only
List only images whose EXIF date taken is
.BR valid ;
see
.BR "EXIF CHECK" .
Implies
.BR "\-\-type image" ,
so videos are not probed, and cannot be combined with
.BR "\-\-type video" .
Unreadable images are left out.
With
.B \-n
only the listed images are renamed.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-kinds " \fIMODE\fR"
.B together
(default) puts videos and images in one output.
.B separate
makes one output per kind: two sections on the screen, and files named
\fIbasename\fR_video.* and \fIbasename\fR_image.*.
A kind with no files produces no output.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-no\-blank\-lines
When ordered by folder, csv and xlsx output normally get an empty row between
folders.
This option leaves them out, giving one unbroken table that is easier to sort and
filter in Excel.
In screen and text output it removes the gap after each folder summary.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-basename " \fINAME\fR"
Base name of output files (default
.BR metadata ).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-delimiter " \fICHAR\fR"
CSV delimiter, a single character (default
.BR , ).
Use
.B ;
for European versions of Excel.
CSV files are written as UTF-8 with a byte order mark.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-overwrite
Overwrite existing output files.
By default an existing file is kept and the output goes to
\fIbasename\fR_01.\fIext\fR, \fIbasename\fR_02.\fIext\fR, and so on.
If the target is locked, for example open in Excel, a new name is used in any case.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-rename
Rename the files to add resolution, and for videos duration, to the name:
.B holiday.mp4
becomes
.BR "holiday (1920x1080 - 0-02-03).mp4" ,
.B photo.jpg
becomes
.BR "photo (4000x3000).jpg" .
Existing files are never overwritten, files that already carry the suffix are skipped,
and failures are reported per file.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-dry\-run
With
.BR \-n :
only show what would be renamed.
.TP
.BI \-\-doubtful\-count " N"
Number of images in a folder above which the doubtful check applies (default 20).
.B 0
switches the check off.
.TP
.BI \-\-doubtful\-seconds " S"
Time span in seconds for the doubtful check (default 60).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Check the prerequisites, show how to install anything missing, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Show the built-in help and exit.
.SH EXIF CHECK
Every image gets an EXIF check of its date taken.
It is
.B valid
unless the date is
.IP \(bu 2
missing, or blank or zero, such as 0000:00:00 00:00:00;
.IP \(bu 2
not understandable as a date;
.IP \(bu 2
before 1990;
.IP \(bu 2
in the future;
.IP \(bu 2
more than one day after the file's creation or modification date, whichever is the
earlier (copying a file changes its creation date, so the modification date is the
safety net).
.PP
A midnight time on a real date is accepted.
.PP
A date that passes is still marked
.B doubtful
when its folder holds more than 20
.RB ( \-\-doubtful\-count )
such images whose dates all lie within 60 seconds
.RB ( \-\-doubtful\-seconds )
of each other, which points to a stuck or reset camera clock or to dates stamped by a
batch tool.
Folders are judged one by one, and only the date taken is compared.
.B \-e
lists only
.B valid
images, so doubtful ones are left out.
.PP
GPS position is always shown when present, as decimal degrees with south and west
negative, plus altitude in metres.
A position that is out of range, or the 0,0 placeholder some devices write, is ignored.
.SH DAMAGED AND MISLABELED FILES
The file content, not the extension, decides how a file is read.
A JPEG named
.B file1.mp4
is reported as an image with a note, and a video named
.B clip.jpg
as a video.
A file whose extension does not match its content is read normally and given a note.
.PP
A file that cannot be read is listed with an error and never stops the run.
This covers files that are locked by another program, have no read permission, are
empty, corrupt or truncated, or take more than 60 seconds to read.
The files with errors are listed again on the terminal when the run ends.
Folders that cannot be read give a warning and the scan continues.
.SH PREREQUISITES
Python 3.8 or newer is always needed.
.TP
.B ffprobe
Part of FFmpeg; needed for video files.
.TP
.B Pillow
Python imaging library; needed for image files.
.TP
.B openpyxl
Needed for Excel output.
.PP
Before any work is done the script checks what is needed and, if something is missing,
stops and prints the install command for the platform, for example
.B "winget install Gyan.FFmpeg"
or
.BR "python \-m pip install pillow openpyxl" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
Files with errors are reported but are not fatal.
.TP
.B 1
A prerequisite is missing, the folder was not found, no matching files were found, or
an output file could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
Bad command line.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl+C.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the current folder on the screen:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Recursive Excel workbook, ordered by folder and then file name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py \-r \-o xlsx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Recursive, ordered by file name only, as a text file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py /data/media \-R \-S name \-o txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Images only, as a CSV file for European Excel:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py \-\-type image \-o csv \-d ";"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Separate Excel files for videos and images:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py \-r \-k separate \-o xlsx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only images with a trustworthy EXIF date:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py \-r \-e \-o xlsx
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview renaming, then do it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
metadata.py \-n \-p
metadata.py \-n
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
\fIbasename\fR.txt, \fIbasename\fR.csv, \fIbasename\fR.xlsx
Output files, written to the current directory.
.SH NOTES
The earlier scripts used different switches.
Mapping:
.B \-N
is now
.BR \-n ,
.B \-O
is now
.BR \-w ,
.BR \-CU / \-CE
are
.B \-o csv
(with
.B \-d ";"
for the European style),
.B \-XLSX
is
.BR "\-o xlsx" ,
and
.B \-S
is now
.BR "\-s name|folder" .
Per-file output files and file-name patterns were dropped in favour of
.BR \-\-type .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.PP
Project page: https://github.com/csternberg/metadata
